% Chapter 62 of the tariff: articles of apparel and clothing accessories, not
% knitted or crocheted — all seventeen headings (6201 to 6217) and their 104
% six-digit subheadings. A library: it includes section_xi.le (the textile
% materials and the notes it shares with Chapter 61), and tariff.le includes
% it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 18 (2026), Chapter 62 notes 1 to 9 and the terms of
% the headings and subheadings (https://hts.usitc.gov/); the subheadings are
% the six-digit HS ones, which the EU Combined Nomenclature shares.
%
% How the headings are read: as in Chapter 61 (chapter_61.le), for articles of
% any textile fabric other than knitted (note 1) — woven, nonwoven, felt, lace.
% Babies' garments go to 6209 (note 5(b)), garments of coated or nonwoven
% fabrics to 6210 (note 6), and 6211 takes the garments no earlier heading
% describes, among them the woven tops that are neither shirts nor blouses.
% Heading 6212 (brassieres, girdles, corsets...) covers them whether or not
% knitted. A scarf no side of which exceeds 60 cm is a handkerchief (note 8).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a group* of *a gender* in *a material* is *a code* under table woven.
    *a good* is of a non-knitted fabric.
    *a good* is made up of nonwovens.

% GRI 6: the six-digit subheadings, as in Chapter 61's table. Heading 6210's
% first subheading (garments of nonwovens, 5602 or 5603) is read by its own
% rule below.
