the knowledge base chapter 62 includes these resources:
    section_xi.

the knowledge base chapter 62 includes:

rule woven_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6217
    and it is not the case that
        the heading = 6210
        and the good is made up of nonwovens
    and the subheading group of the good is a group
    and the gender of the good is a gender
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component has a fabric for heading the heading
    and the fibre material of the component is a material
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the group of the gender in the material is the code under table woven.

rule woven_subheading_6210_10 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Of fabrics of heading 5602 or 5603":
the subheading of a good in heading 6210 is "6210.10"
    if the good is made up of nonwovens.

% the first subheading of heading 6210: garments of felt or nonwovens
rule subheading_6210_10 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Of fabrics of heading 5602 or 5603":
a good is made up of nonwovens
    if the good is made up of fabric of heading a heading
    and the heading is in [5602, 5603].

% Note 1: made up articles of any textile fabric other than wadding, excluding
% knitted or crocheted articles
rule note_62_1 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "This chapter applies only to made up articles of any textile fabric other than wadding, excluding knitted or crocheted articles (other than those of heading 6212)":
a good is of a non-knitted fabric
    if the construction of the good is a construction
    and the construction is in [woven, nonwoven, felt, lace].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule heading_6201 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windbreakers and similar articles (including padded, sleeveless jackets), other than those of heading 6203":
a garment is described by heading 6201
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the family of the garment is outerwear.

rule heading_6202 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Women's or girls' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski jackets), windbreakers and similar articles (including padded, sleeveless jackets), other than those of heading 6204":
a garment is described by heading 6202
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the family of the garment is outerwear.

rule heading_6203 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Men's or boys' suits, ensembles, suit-type jackets, blazers, trousers, bib and brace overalls, breeches and shorts (other than swimwear)":
a garment is described by heading 6203
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the subheading group of the garment is a group
    and the group is in [suit, ensemble, suit-type jacket, trousers].

rule heading_6204 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Women's or girls' suits, ensembles, suit-type jackets, blazers, dresses, skirts, divided skirts, trousers, bib and brace overalls, breeches and shorts (other than swimwear)":
a garment is described by heading 6204
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the subheading group of the garment is a group
    and the group is in [suit, ensemble, suit-type jacket, dress, skirt, trousers].

% Chapter 62 note 1: articles other than knitted or crocheted
rule heading_6205 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Men's or boys' shirts":
a garment is described by heading 6205
    if the construction of the garment is woven
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the garment is a shirt.

rule heading_6206 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Women's or girls' blouses, shirts and shirt-blouses":
a garment is described by heading 6206
    if the construction of the garment is woven
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the garment is a blouse-type garment.

rule heading_6207 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Men's or boys' singlets and other undershirts, underpants, briefs, nightshirts, pajamas, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles":
a garment is described by heading 6207
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [undershirt, underpants, nightwear, robe].

rule heading_6208 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Women's or girls' singlets and other undershirts, slips, petticoats, briefs, panties, nightdresses, pajamas, negligees, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles":
a garment is described by heading 6208
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [undershirt, slip, underpants, nightwear, robe].

rule heading_6209 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Babies' garments and clothing accessories":
a good is described by heading 6209
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the good is sized for babies.

rule heading_6210 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Garments, made up of fabrics of heading 5602, 5603, 5903, 5906 or 5907":
a garment is described by heading 6210
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the garment is a garment
    and the garment is made up of coated fabric.

% the woven tops that are neither shirts nor blouses are "other garments"
rule heading_6211 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Track suits, ski-suits and swimwear; other garments":
a garment is described by heading 6211
    if the garment is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the garment is a garment.

rule heading_6212 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Brassieres, girdles, corsets, braces, suspenders, garters and similar articles and parts thereof, whether or not knitted or crocheted":
a good is described by heading 6212
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [brassiere, girdle, corset, braces].

rule heading_6213 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Handkerchiefs":
a good is described by heading 6213
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the subheading group of the good is handkerchief.

rule heading_6214 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Shawls, scarves, mufflers, mantillas, veils and the like":
a good is described by heading 6214
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the subheading group of the good is scarf.

rule heading_6215 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Ties, bow ties and cravats":
a good is described by heading 6215
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the family of the good is tie.

rule heading_6216 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Gloves, mittens and mitts":
a good is described by heading 6216
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the family of the good is gloves.

rule heading_6217 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Other made up clothing accessories; parts of garments or of clothing accessories, other than those of heading 6212":
a good is described by heading 6217
    if the good is of a non-knitted fabric
    and the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [other accessory, part].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Choosing between headings that both describe a good (GRI 3(a) in gri.le).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule note_62_5b_before with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Articles which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6209 and in other headings of this chapter are to be classified in heading 6209":
heading 6209 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6208.

rule note_62_5b_after with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Articles which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6209 and in other headings of this chapter are to be classified in heading 6209":
heading 6209 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6210
    and the heading <= 6217.

rule note_62_6_before with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Garments which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6210 and in other headings of this chapter, excluding heading 6209, are to be classified in heading 6210":
heading 6210 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6208.

rule note_62_6_after with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Garments which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6210 and in other headings of this chapter, excluding heading 6209, are to be classified in heading 6210":
heading 6210 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6211
    and the heading <= 6217.

% Heading 6211 ("other garments") covers what the headings before it do not.
rule gri_3a_6211 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 6211
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6208.
